# Multikernel network device configuration
#

config MULTIKERNEL_ETH
	tristate "Virtual Ethernet between multikernel instances"
	depends on MULTIKERNEL
	help
	  Presents a normal Ethernet device, mk0, in every kernel instance
	  and carries frames between them over multikernel's shared-memory
	  IPI ring. Unmodified AF_INET applications can then talk across the
	  kernel boundary, which AF_VSOCK alone does not allow.

	  The link is point-to-point: a spawn talks to instance 0, and the
	  host to the instance named by the "peer" module parameter.
	  Addresses are left to userspace; bring mk0 up with ip(8) as for
	  any other interface.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module will
	  be called mk_eth. If unsure, say N.
